{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-81708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=-\\frac{4}{(2+t)^{2}}$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, find the velocity (in $\\text{m}/\\text{s}$) of the particle at time $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-81708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{4}{(2+t)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2+t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{4}{2+0}+C \\\\ 2 & =2+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{4}{2+t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-81708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e7787218132b17bffca1231384c8545f0b02c15b247e94cc5489cdf213ed24c"} {"question" "q-81708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-81708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "v(t)=\\frac{16}{(2+t)^{3}}"] ["math" "v(t)=\\frac{2}{2+t}+1"] ["math" "v(t)=\\frac{4}{2+t}"] ["math" "v(t)=\\frac{4}{2+t}+2"] ["math" "v(t)=\\frac{8}{(2+t)^{3}}+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-81708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(t)=\\frac{4}{2+t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-102694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=8-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-\\frac{5}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-102694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (8-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8t-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=-\\frac{5}{2}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2} & =8(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{3}+C \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & =0+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=8t-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=3\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =8(3)-\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{3}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =24-\\frac{27}{2}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =24-16 \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $8\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-102694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e7787218132b17bffca1231384c8545f0b02c15b247e94cc5489cdf213ed24c"} {"question" "q-102694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-102694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "14\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "16\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "4\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "8\\,\\text{m/s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-102694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-346883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=12{t}^{5}+5{t}^{4},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=6\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-346883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (12{t}^{5}+5{t}^{4})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{6}+{t}^{5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=6.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =2({1}^{6})+{1}^{5}+C \\\\ 6 & =3+C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=2{t}^{6}+{t}^{5}+3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-346883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e7787218132b17bffca1231384c8545f0b02c15b247e94cc5489cdf213ed24c"} {"question" "q-346883" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-346883" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2t^6+t^5+3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-351053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in ${\\text{ft/s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=8t+{e}^{t-2},$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{ft/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=5\\,\\text{ft/s}$ when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-351053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (8t+{e}^{t-2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}+{e}^{t-2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(2)=5.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =4({2}^{2})+{e}^{2-2}+C \\\\ 5 & =16+1+C \\\\ 5 & =17+C \\\\ C & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=4{t}^{2}+{e}^{t-2}-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-351053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e7787218132b17bffca1231384c8545f0b02c15b247e94cc5489cdf213ed24c"} {"question" "q-351053" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-351053" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4t^2+e^{t-2}-12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-351058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=5{e}^{t},$ where $a(t)$ is measured in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the speed of the particle at the moment $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{s}$ given that the particle has velocity $v=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$\n\nThe speed at the moment $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n{{field-1}} $\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-351058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 5{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{e}^{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =5{e}^{0}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =5+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=5{e}^{t}-\\frac{9}{2}.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{s}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =5{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =5(2)-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{2}-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $\\frac{11}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-351058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e7787218132b17bffca1231384c8545f0b02c15b247e94cc5489cdf213ed24c"} {"question" "q-351058" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da150a56350d79be5320b5db626dec83194db7420e52e768c3fb68c5b534f96"} {"question" "q-351058" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031307/state.json" "file_sha256" "8da1